#### Archivo 4: El compilador automático de GitHub (`build-apk.yml`)
1. Abre un nuevo **Bloc de notas**.
2. Copia este código:
```yaml:GitHub Actions Workflow:.github/workflows/build-apk.yml
name: Build Android APK

on:
  push:
    branches: [ "main" ]
  workflow_dispatch:

jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:
      - name: Checkout del repositorio
        uses: actions/checkout@v4

      - name: Configurar Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'

      - name: Configurar Java JDK 17
        uses: actions/setup-java@v4
        with:
          distribution: 'zulu'
          java-version: '17'

      - name: Instalar dependencias
        run: npm install

      - name: Inicializar Capacitor Android
        run: npx cap add android

      - name: Sincronizar Capacitor
        run: npx cap sync

      - name: Construir el APK
        working-directory: ./android
        run: |
          chmod +x gradlew
          ./gradlew assembleDebug

      - name: Subir el APK
        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
        with:
          name: NuestraBoda-APK
          path: android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk
```
3. Guárdalo dentro de la carpeta `.github/workflows/` con el nombre exacto: `build-apk.yml`

